You're barking up a tree that I already peed on :-P  I've already done
what you've outlined yesterday.  What's happening is this: the tools are
running, but segfaulting when they hit the exit() call.  I'm building the
libs with debugging now to see if I can figure out what's going on.  FYI,
with your installed qt2.2, try running one of their tutorials or
examples.  They all exhibit the same behaviour (segfault on exit, but they
run fine otherwise).

To anyone else who is looking into this, you need to edit the
configs/linux-* files and remove '-O2' for Alpha.  Seems that we run into
an optimiser bug when compiling.  I'm *not* discounting the source,
though, WRT that bug.  MANY times, I've found that there is a problem in
the code that causes gcc to exit with an ICE.  I'm just trying to exhaust
all options before looking at the code (since it's quite a few lines to
peruse).

C




