Hi,


> Hi folks,
>
> It's planning time here, and I am trying to find a rough price estimate, and
> reliable supplier, for a machine where the main requirement is a large amount
> of RAM, namely 8GB.

I've got a URL lying around for exactly such occasions -
http://www.digital.com/info/LIW0Q7/LIW0Q7SC.TXT
It claims $39,934 for the ES40 with 1 CPU/512 MB (and OpenVMS,
peanuts comparing to the price of the iron).

8GB is going to be VERY expensive (I recently bought 4 GB computer :-) and
also was looking for such kind of info). Even refurbished components
from
http://www.compaqworks.com/cwstore/templates/products/Alpha_server_info.asp
list (supposing that price for the ES40 memory will be similar)
B2-MS7CC-GA Alpha server 8xxx 4 GB $30,000

>
>
> The whole (well, pretty much) of the RAM must be available for one process, so
> only a 64-bit machine (and OS) is adequate.

I don't know what kind of problems you have in mind, I'm running what basically
is add/multiply calculations with 4GB array and I would say that one 400MHz CPU
is not enough for this amount of data at all.

>
> I already got some quotes from Sun and SGI, but it seems I have a hard time
