With regards to your message at 12:28 PM 9/15/00, Patrick Greene. Where you 
stated:
>Two questions you experts can help an old Amiga guy with on Red Hat 6.2 
>(which I am new to - As well as Alpha)
>
>I have a PC64 motherboard (275mhz) with 64 megs ram,
>I have a Adaptec 2942UW2 in addition to the onboard IDE,
>I have installed RH 6.2 using MILO and have been running it for a few weeks.
>
>Question one: Do you think SRM will recognize my SCSI card?
No.
Something like a decent Symbios Logic based card would be best.
The Intraserver 3140U works well, for example.
I have one of those in our PC164/EB64/Cabriolet box here.


>I am using a 4 meg Matrox Millenium card, but would like to get a card 
>that has more ram and updates better under Linux on the alpha. My main 
>concern is 2D, however, 3D is a plus
>
>Question Two:  Please recommend a card that would suit my purpose.
Matrox G200 PCI
Elsa Gloria Synergy PCI



