With regards to your message at 05:38 AM 9/18/00, Steven N. Hirsch. Where 
you stated:
>On Sun, 17 Sep 2000, W Bauske wrote:
>
> > SRM does see Tekram DC390F cards on my systems. I think Tru64 doesn't
> > use it well though, something about using only 810 type instructions.
> >
> > This card will probably work but I haven't bought one so you're
> > on your own. It is an original Symbios card. Only $39 each so
> > it's not too painful.
> >
> > http://www.centrix-intl.com/8251s.htm
>
>I'll second this recommendation.  Their card is recognized by SRM and
>Tru64 5.0.  The latter bitches about "unsupported chip" on boot but runs
>fine.
>
>Steve
Depends on your definition of "fine".
If you are running one device on the card, and it is a 7200rpm or slower 
device, this will keep up.
However it will NOT as anything other than a dumb, 8 bit SCSI, no SCSI 
scripting, and most importantly only SCSI FAST, not UltraSCSI.
20MB/sec max on wide devices, rather than the 40/sec the chip is capable of.


