On Fri, 22 Sep 2000 AWM@inel.gov wrote:

> I am configuring 15 Personal Work Station 500a's as a Beowulf Cluster.  I
> am not new to Linux but am not what you would call an expert by any means.
> I wonder if someone could give me some information on where I can find how
> to configure these machines so the console is on a serial port, as they
> need to boot without a graphics monitor.  (Some direction to information
> describing Beowulf Clusters would be welcomed and appreciated also.)
> Thanks!

look at /usr/src/linux/Documentation/serial-console.txt
generaly add "console=ttyS0" to you boot string and you are off and
running.

